"""Village Residential Street Scene. One scene ID; zero new standalone models.

Blender 4.3+; metres, Z up. Run:
  blender -b -t 4 --python-exit-code 1 --python generate.py -- --no-render
  blender -b -t 4 --python-exit-code 1 --python generate.py -- --render-gray
  blender -b -t 4 --python-exit-code 1 --python generate.py -- --render-final
Only this generator is required; the exact fixed original sources, four native
files and five actual GLBs are embedded and hash checked. No remote access.
The cottage executes only its original geometric construction prefix in a fresh
scene (the original native exceeded connector inline transfer size). Other
models append only explicitly named mesh objects from fixed native bytes. No
old native script, camera, light, handler, linked library or studio is executed.

Four unchanged cottages face a nine-tile soil lane; pitch 2.002m preserves the
original documented 2mm real seams. Narrow stone border straight MEMBER only
is reused, leaving four 2.004m front gaps. It is not the whole two-member kit.
Eight detached full fence panels retain their terminal posts, with 41.6mm gaps
between adjacent pairs. Two original fruit trees mark the middle garden gaps.
All placements are rigid, unit scale. External flat game ground at Z=0 is
required under house foundations, tree roots, fence feet, road and borders.
Road shoulder .02m meets the original cottage step front after a 2mm horizontal
gap; first tread .13m means an approximately .11m rise (bevels retained).
Fixed solid doors are not operable and no enterable interiors are claimed.
This is static visual scenery, not navigation, vehicle routing, collision,
accessibility, architectural, structural or safety certification.
"""
